      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix incorrect `next_tokens` parameter in NPU graph decode mode that was causing wrong attention computation for sliding-window attention layers.\n\n## Problem\n\nIn `forward_decode_graph` method of `ascend_backend.py`, the `next_tokens` parameter logic was inverted:\n- SWA layers incorrectly received `FULL_ATTENTION_WINDOW` (2147483647) instead of 0\n- This caused incorrect attention computation in graph decode mode\n- The non-graph decode path correctly uses `next_tokens=0` for all cases\n\n## Solution\n\nChanged `next_tokens` parameter to always be 0 in graph decode mode, matching the non-graph decode path behavior.\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nnext_tokens=(\n    0 if layer.sliding_window_size == -1 else FULL_ATTENTION_WINDOW\n),\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nnext_tokens=0,\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n- Existing unit test at `test/registered/unit/npu/attention/test_npu_ascend_backend.py:584` already validates `assert kwargs[\"next_tokens\"] == 0`\n- Syntax validation passed\n- Note: Full validation requires NPU hardware\n\n## Impact\n\n- Fixes incorrect attention computation for SWA models in NPU graph decode mode\n- Minimal change (1 line modified, 3 lines removed)\n- No breaking changes to API or behavior\n\nFixes #47399\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41164590214](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41164590214)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41164590235](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41164590235)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41164590171](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41164590171)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
